 :org/region-primary :region-middle-east
 :org/countries ["MY" "SA" "ID" "FR" "JP" "GB"]
 :org/founding-date 1800
 :org/founding-note "British friendly societies and continental mutuelles predate state insurance; modern takaful was formalized from the 1970s."
 :org/member-count-basis "unknown in aggregate — takaful operators publish premiums rather than member counts, Japanese 共済 report subscriber numbers in the tens of millions across JA/JCCU/labour schemes, and French mutuelles cover a large share of complementary health insurance. No comparable global membership figure exists."
 :org/legal-registration :registered
 :org/registration-note "Registered as insurers, but the legal form encodes a community claim: policyholders are members and surplus returns to them rather than to shareholders."
 :org/governance-model :democratic
 :org/mission-statement "Risk pooled among members who own the pool — the institutional descendant of burial societies and ROSCAs, scaled up and regulated, and the point where mutual aid becomes an industry."
